Patch: ViRMEn 2016-02-12  bin/gui/updateFigures.m  -- list Linux mex files

The GUI builds its movement and transformation menus from platform-specific
mex files, with cases for PCWIN / PCWIN64 / MACI64 but none for GLNXA64. On
Linux the transformation list comes back empty and the GUI crashes at startup:

  Index exceeds matrix dimensions.
  Error in updateFigures (line 494)
          handles.exper.transformationFunction = str2func(str{1});

Add a GLNXA64 case in BOTH blocks.

--- movements block (~line 455) ---
         case 'MACI64'
             mf = [mf; dir([path filesep '..' filesep '..' filesep 'movements' filesep '*.mexmaci64'])];
+        case 'GLNXA64'
+            mf = [mf; dir([path filesep '..' filesep '..' filesep 'movements' filesep '*.mexa64'])];
     end

--- transformations block (~line 480) ---
         case 'MACI64'
             mf = [mf; dir([path filesep '..' filesep '..' filesep 'transformations' filesep '*.mexmaci64'])];
+        case 'GLNXA64'
+            mf = [mf; dir([path filesep '..' filesep '..' filesep 'transformations' filesep '*.mexa64'])];
     end

Verify:  grep -c "GLNXA64" bin/gui/updateFigures.m    -> 2
Then in MATLAB: clear functions; rehash
